WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.023
Small airway reopening can produce rapid fluid

00:00:04.023 --> 00:00:04.702
stresses.

00:00:04.702 --> 00:00:08.705
Direct observation inside a whole lung is difficult to

00:00:08.705 --> 00:00:09.595
standardise.

00:00:14.675 --> 00:00:18.484
A parallel-plate flow chamber permits controlled fluid

00:00:18.484 --> 00:00:22.294
motion over a monolayer. This simplified geometry is a

00:00:22.294 --> 00:00:23.634
modelling decision.

00:00:28.675 --> 00:00:32.355
The published method uses a flow-induced stress event

00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:32.494
to

00:00:32.494 --> 00:00:35.699
study damage to cells under controlled exposure

00:00:35.699 --> 00:00:36.450
conditions.

00:00:40.967 --> 00:00:44.619
Fluorescence-based injury measurements must be timed,

00:00:44.619 --> 00:00:48.340
controlled and interpreted with care. A signal is not

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:48.410
a

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:50.202
complete injury mechanism.

00:00:55.383 --> 00:00:59.136
The chamber isolates a mechanical challenge. It does

00:00:59.136 --> 00:00:59.353
not

00:00:59.353 --> 00:01:02.827
recreate airway anatomy, immune dynamics or every

00:01:02.827 --> 00:01:04.812
interaction in a human lung.

00:01:10.092 --> 00:01:13.841
A reproducible instrument turns an invisible question

00:01:13.841 --> 00:01:17.449
into a measurable experiment. The paper records its

00:01:17.449 --> 00:01:19.360
operating logic and limits.
